 "notes": "Observed 95% c.l. COBE/FIRAS limit on dark photon kinetic mixing epsilon vs mass m_d, from the solid blue 'FIRAS CosmoTherm' curve of Fig. 8 (file eps/eps_limits_new.pdf in the e-print), recovered from the vector paths with axis calibration against the tick labels. This is the paper's headline result: a new FIRAS bound computed with CosmoTherm including photon-number changes and the large-distortion regime (uses |Delta rho/rho| < 6e-5 at 95% c.l.). The dashed analytic estimate, the PIXIE curve (projection) and the McDermott & Witte 2020 comparison curve were not used. Limit derives from CMB photon -> dark photon conversion, so no local dark-matter density is assumed. epsilon is reported directly (chi, not chi^2).",
